---
title: Basket
render: static
---
<!--
  The basket screen — a prerendered SHELL with one island in it.

  There is no `load()` and there must not be. Every other static route here
  reads the database at build time and bakes the answer into the file; a basket
  belongs to one shopper and is reached by a token this browser holds, so there
  is nothing about it that could be baked and nothing about it a CDN may cache.
  What ships is the heading below and an island marker.

  That is also why there is no `publishes:` and no gate question to answer: the
  build taps the Litestone client while `load()` runs, and this route runs none.
-->
<script>
  import Basket from '../../islands/Basket.mesa'
</script>

<div class="container">
  <!--
    The <noscript> is BESIDE the island and not inside it, and that is not a
    style choice: an island with element children hangs the prerender pass with
    no output at all (`FJS-549`). An island's markup is replaced wholesale on
    mount anyway — it is a marker, not a slot — so there was never a way for
    children to survive it.
  -->
  <noscript>
    <h1>Basket</h1>
    <p>Your basket needs JavaScript. <a class="link" href="/catalog/">Back to the catalogue</a>.</p>
  </noscript>

  <Basket client:load />
</div>
